{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793793795,"nonce":"c5I1EntnHAxEeV1D9G7uMPYURpY=","message":"Implemented pending-error rewrite batching. thread now rebuilds predecessor/successor lists once after applying the planned edges, before the unchanged dominance check. Both thread and bypass_merges retain only affected phis and terminators for rollback; they no longer clone the whole block/instruction graph. Rollback reconstructs the CFG. The rewrite decisions, dominance rejection, optimization pipeline, and tiering policy are unchanged.\n\nAdded a 64-edge phi/CFG regression test (also passed on the original implementation) and a rollback test checking phi/edge restoration and preservation of instruction storage. The held root-registry experiment was excluded from both benchmark arms; its patch remains archived and uncommitted.\n\nNUC before/after against 68b4de44b6f9c8f2fcd38b3808caf07fdddb9c03, ordinary frozen release binaries with LLVM enabled, taskset 0,2,4,6. Builds and diagnostic traces finished before cooldown and timing. Same thermal/load gate as prior work: initial minimum 60 seconds and 20 consecutive acceptable seconds; before each sample package \u003c=60 C, core \u003c=65 C, total busy \u003c=0.75 CPU cores and benchmark physical cores including SMT \u003c=0.5. No Cargo/rustc during completed timed batches.\n\nmethod_call: 21 alternating samples per arm, median wall 31.569 -\u003e 29.902 ms (5.3% lower); kernel 3.675 -\u003e 3.662 ms (effectively unchanged). No throttled samples. Untimed per-pass trace: error_flag total for the chunk 1.11 -\u003e 0.87 ms. A traced pass timing is not a complete additive explanation of the wall-time delta.\n\nFull suite: all 17 Lua and 22 supported Python kernels completed and matched output/checksum checks. Seven samples per arm for other kernels. Lua geometric mean baseline/candidate wall ratio 1.00174x; Python clean-case ratio 1.00231x: overall flat, not a broad suite win. hexiom2 and nqueens throttled and are excluded from clean speed comparisons. pidigits remains unsupported.\n\nThe initial records row was 82.727 -\u003e 84.991 ms (2.7% slower). A separate 21-round clean repeat was 83.467 -\u003e 83.400 ms, no throttling: the slowdown did not reproduce. Two preceding repeat attempts aborted when unrelated Rayde Cargo jobs appeared; they are preserved separately and not mixed into the accepted repeat. Those jobs were left untouched.\n\nValidation after the full benchmark suite: 19 compiler error_flag unit tests passed; 56 Lua regression test functions passed (46 conformance categories/harness checks including official portable/full configurations and warm-up variants, plus 10 receiver/field/resume tests). Lua existing known-failure expectations are unchanged; this is regression validation, not a claim of full Lua compatibility. Clippy -D warnings, cargo fmt --check and git diff --check passed.\n\nTypeScript: 1413 local execution checks passed across interpreter, baseline and LLVM profiles. Complete pinned official corpus: 5948/5948 source files, 6825 expanded rows, PASS 1151 / FAIL 12 / UNSUPPORTED 2234 / SKIP 3428, regressions []. Final report binary SHA-256 matches target/release/zynode. Reviewed baseline unchanged; existing failures, unsupported cases and skips are not passes.\n\nEvidence: /private/tmp/zyntax-first-use/ (local build/test/conformance reports) and zyntax-first-use-evidence.tar.gz there (NUC scripts, raw samples, thermal logs, binary hashes, source patch, traces and interrupted repeats). Archive SHA-256 de38c195e2bbd4d3b6789f60d39541bceaf904cda76ee37cac6b4cc6ec9969b6. NUC original checkout and tracked/untracked contents restored and verified; task scratch removed. No push.\n\nThe broader first-entry wait and interpreter-first/OSR issues remain open. This change only removes avoidable compiler work on that path.","files":null}]}